### Core Principles (from Superpowers)

- **TDD** — No production code without a failing test first
- **YAGNI** — Don't build what isn't needed yet
- **DRY** — Don't repeat yourself
- **Systematic > Ad-hoc** — Process over guessing
- **Evidence > Claims** — Verify before declaring success
- **Root cause > Symptoms** — Fix the source, not the surface

## Project-Specific Rules

### Tech Stack
- Next.js 15 (App Router)
- React 19
- TypeScript (strict)
- Tailwind CSS 4 (@theme syntax)
- No external API dependencies for MVP

### Content Rules
- 义理派立场 — 不做占卜，只做情境模式匹配
- 内容编写规范见 `docs/CONTENT-GUIDE.md`
- 字符串内嵌引号统一用「」，不用英文双引号

### Code Style
- Chinese-first UI text, i18n-ready architecture
- Prefer font-serif for classical content, font-sans for UI chrome
- CSS variables for all colors (--color-ink-*, --color-vermillion, --color-gold)
- Components in `components/`, hooks in `hooks/`, types in `lib/types.ts`

### Plans & Documentation
- Implementation plans go to `docs/superpowers/plans/`
- Design specs go to `docs/superpowers/specs/`
- Keep plans granular: 2-5 min per task step

### Git Conventions
- Commit messages: `feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`, `test:`, `chore:`
- Frequent small commits over large batches
- Branch naming: `feat/<name>`, `fix/<name>`, `refactor/<name>`
